        <argsstring>(ModTypeId modTypeId)</argsstring>
        <name>getModType</name>
        <qualifiedname>AGRemapCore::ModTypeIdTools::getModType</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="namespace_a_g_remap_core_1aa5ba53a4a6662429047abb6750bbbd2f" kindref="member">ModTypeId</ref></type>
          <declname>modTypeId</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
Retrieves the :cpp:class:`ModType` registered for a :cpp:enum:`ModTypeId`, if one has
been registered (via :cpp:func:`registerModType`) :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

This is a plain lookup into a global registry shared by every caller of
:cpp:class:`ModTypeIdTools` -- it never builds a :cpp:class:`ModType` itself. If a
:cpp:enum:`ModTypeId` is never registered, nothing is ever built for it, since building
one can be expensive; only a :cpp:enum:`ModTypeId` that&apos;s actually been registered
(typically by whichever builder -- e.g. ``GIBuilder`` -- actually owns it) can be
retrieved here
</verbatim></para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>modTypeId</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The :cpp:enum:<computeroutput><ref refid="namespace_a_g_remap_core_1aa5ba53a4a6662429047abb6750bbbd2f" kindref="member">ModTypeId</ref></computeroutput> to retrieve the registered :cpp:class:<computeroutput><ref refid="class_a_g_remap_core_1_1_mod_type" kindref="compound">ModType</ref></computeroutput> for</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The registered :cpp:class:<computeroutput><ref refid="class_a_g_remap_core_1_1_mod_type" kindref="compound">ModType</ref></computeroutput>, if one exists for &apos;modTypeId&apos; </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
