      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="function" id="class_a_g_remap_core_1_1_mod_type_id_tools_1ad7161ca8d4908f7c9aa0d1a6c7c5a8e5" prot="public" static="yes" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void AGRemapCore::ModTypeIdTools::registerModType</definition>
        <argsstring>(const ModType &amp;modType)</argsstring>
        <name>registerModType</name>
        <qualifiedname>AGRemapCore::ModTypeIdTools::registerModType</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const <ref refid="class_a_g_remap_core_1_1_mod_type" kindref="compound">ModType</ref> &amp;</type>
          <declname>modType</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
Registers a :cpp:class:`ModType` into the global registry, under the
:cpp:enum:`ModTypeId` it owns (``modType.modTypeId``) :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

If a :cpp:class:`ModType` is already registered for that :cpp:enum:`ModTypeId`, it gets
overwritten with the new one
</verbatim></para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>modType</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The :cpp:class:<computeroutput><ref refid="class_a_g_remap_core_1_1_mod_type" kindref="compound">ModType</ref></computeroutput> to register </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
