      <memberdef kind="function" id="class_a_g_remap_core_1_1_mod_type_id_tools_1ac1b5b4a67cb332ba516679975ce45443" prot="public" static="yes" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>std::optional&lt; <ref refid="namespace_a_g_remap_core_1aa5ba53a4a6662429047abb6750bbbd2f" kindref="member">ModTypeId</ref> &gt;</type>
        <definition>std::optional&lt; ModTypeId &gt; AGRemapCore::ModTypeIdTools::findByName</definition>
        <argsstring>(const std::string &amp;name, std::optional&lt; GameTypeId &gt; gameTypeId=std::nullopt)</argsstring>
        <name>findByName</name>
        <qualifiedname>AGRemapCore::ModTypeIdTools::findByName</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const std::string &amp;</type>
          <declname>name</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>std::optional&lt; <ref refid="namespace_a_g_remap_core_1a3cec628c65b87e9eae2e12e5fd01768f" kindref="member">GameTypeId</ref> &gt;</type>
          <declname>gameTypeId</declname>
          <defval>std::nullopt</defval>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
Finds the :cpp:enum:`ModTypeId` whose registered :cpp:class:`ModType` name or alias
maximally matches some string, similar to how :cpp:func:`IniClassifier::readSectionName`
searches ``sectionKeywordsDFA`` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

Only searches names/aliases of :cpp:class:`ModType` s that have actually been registered
via :cpp:func:`registerModType` -- an unregistered :cpp:enum:`ModTypeId` can never be
found this way, even if &apos;name&apos; textually matches what :cpp:func:`getName` would return
for it :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

If more than one registered :cpp:enum:`ModTypeId` shares the maximally-matched name (or
alias) -- after filtering by &apos;gameTypeId&apos;, when given -- the match is ambiguous and
``std::nullopt`` is returned rather than guessing
</verbatim></para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>name</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The string to search for a registered :cpp:class:<computeroutput><ref refid="class_a_g_remap_core_1_1_mod_type" kindref="compound">ModType</ref></computeroutput> name/alias within </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>gameTypeId</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
If provided, only considers a :cpp:class:`ModType` registered under this
:cpp:enum:`GameTypeId` (via ``modType.gameTypeId``) a candidate match
</verbatim></para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The matched :cpp:enum:<computeroutput><ref refid="namespace_a_g_remap_core_1aa5ba53a4a6662429047abb6750bbbd2f" kindref="member">ModTypeId</ref></computeroutput>, if exactly one unambiguous match was found </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
