      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="function" id="class_a_g_remap_core_1_1_mod_type_id_tools_1a52e631f033758e9dca14f1ad79e4731f" prot="public" static="yes" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void AGRemapCore::ModTypeIdTools::clear</definition>
        <argsstring>()</argsstring>
        <name>clear</name>
        <qualifiedname>AGRemapCore::ModTypeIdTools::clear</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
Clears the global registry -- every :cpp:class:`ModType` registered via
:cpp:func:`registerModType` is forgotten, and :cpp:func:`getModType`/
:cpp:func:`findByName` behave as if nothing was ever registered :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

Mirrors ``HashTools``/``CppHashTools``&apos;s own ``clear()`` -- meant for resetting shared
global state between independent uses (e.g. between unit tests)
</verbatim> </para>
        </detaileddescription>
